  "result": "Excellent! All 346 tests pass. The bulk discount feature is complete. Here's what I implemented:\n\n**Updated `src/totals.js`:**\n\n**Enhanced `lineDiscount(line)` function:**\n- Calculates regular discount first: `qty \u00d7 unitPrice \u00d7 discountPercent / 100`\n- For lines with qty \u2265 10, applies extra 2.5% bulk discount to the amount after regular discount\n- Formula: `bulkDiscount = (amountAfterRegular) \u00d7 0.025` (rounded with banker's rounding)\n- Returns total: `regularDiscount + bulkDiscount`\n\n**How it works:**\n1. Regular discount applied first (tier or explicit)\n2. Bulk discount (2.5%) applied to remainder if qty \u2265 10\n3. VAT calculated on amount after ALL discounts\n4. Both discounts included in invoiceTotals discount field\n\n**Examples:**\n- qty=9, price=1000, discount=5%: No bulk discount (qty < 10)\n- qty=10, price=1000, discount=0%: Bulk discount = 1000 \u00d7 2.5% = 25\n- qty=10, price=1000, discount=5%: Regular=50, then bulk=(950 \u00d7 2.5%)=24, total=74\n\n**Added 17 comprehensive tests covering:**\n- No bulk discount for qty < 10\n- Bulk discount for qty \u2265 10\n- Bulk discount after regular discount\n- Bulk discount with tier discounts\n- VAT calculated correctly after bulk discount\n- invoiceTotals includes bulk in discount field\n- Multiple lines with/without bulk discount\n- Fractional cent rounding\n- Large quantities\n- Integration with createInvoice\n\n**Test Results:** 346 passing (all tests including 17 new bulk discount tests).\n\nThe feature seamlessly integrates with existing discount and VAT systems while maintaining full backward compatibility.",
